<title>USA: GM gets favorable IRS ruling on spin-off.</title>
<headline>GM gets favorable IRS ruling on spin-off.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp Tuesday said it received a ruling from the Internal Revenue Service on Monday that GM's contemplated spin-off of the Hughes defense business would be tax-free to GM and its stockholders.</p>
<p>In a statement accompanying Hughes Electronics Corp's second quarter financial results, GM said the spin-off of the Hughes defense business to holders of GM $1-2/3 par value, and GM Class H common stocks, and its subsequent merger with Raytheon Co, are part of a series of related transactions announced by GM and Hughes in January.</p>
</text>
